                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237494327",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198204936247",
                            "num_reviews": 8,
                            "playtime_forever": 218,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 218,
                            "last_played": 1791743494
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Every review of Ikaruga comes down to these two points\n1. It is a beautiful game, a great game, something that you could use as a textbook example of what a good game is.\n2. Good luck beating the game unless you use infinite continues. \n\nObviously there is a lot more to say in depth about this game, from how the polarity system works, how each stage is designed, and more but I can say that apart from the obvious (it's hard, they are really fun to go through especially as you figure out what you need to do to get the max chain score, or even just to survive. I'm not sure if this is the HARDEST Shmup, but I can see why it has the reputation for sure. \n\nIf anything, the difficulty only enhances the game with the short text blurbs about needing to achieve perfection, which is where the game really shines. If you haven't played it, give it a shot. You might not be able to even make it to stage 3 without getting a game over, but it certainly feels rewarding to master it.",
